a31aed243923cb8d4e7caf8a1dc8b8bc6fb8ab6d7e93ba1","caption":"Coating QDs with denaturated BSA. temperature: 60 °C. duration: 30 min. Recipe-level reported vessel: three-neck flask. No vessel assignment is made for this step. Conceptual action diagram. Arrows indicate an action only; no apparatus detail is inferred.","source_locator":"Main PDF p.3"}]},"presentation_status":"pending","general_background":[{"id":"hot-injection","title":"Injection and precursor supply","summary":"Rapid injection can concentrate precursor conversion near the start of a reaction, helping distinguish nucleation from subsequent growth. A short period of rapid precursor conversion can favour nucleation, while a later lower supply can favour growth on existing particles.","label":"General background, not the authors' interpretation","reference":{"doi":"10.1021/cr400544s","url":"https://doi.org/10.1021/cr400544s","kind":"review","title":"Mechanisms of Nucleation and Growth of Nanoparticles in Solution","container":"Chemical Reviews","year":2014}},{"id":"carboxylate-ligand","title":"Carboxylic-acid and carboxylate ligands","summary":"Carboxylic acids and carboxylates can associate with metal-containing surfaces and solution species through their oxygen groups. The hydrocarbon part of a long-chain ligand can favour dispersion in a compatible solvent, while acid-base equilibria influence how its head group associates.","label":"General background, not the authors' interpretation","reference":{"doi":"10.1021/cr900137k","url":"https://doi.org/10.1021/cr900137k","kind":"review","title":"Prospects of Colloidal Nanocrystals for Electronic and Optoelectronic Applications","container":"Chemical Reviews","year":2009}},{"id":"amine-ligand","title":"Amine coordination","summary":"An amine nitrogen can donate electron density to suitable solution species or surface sites. Donation from the nitrogen lone pair and competition with other ligands can change precursor speciation and surface association.","label":"General background, not the authors' interpretation","reference":{"doi":"10.1021/cr900137k","url":"https://doi.org/10.1021/cr900137k","kind":"review","title":"Prospects of Colloidal Nanocrystals for Electronic and Optoelectronic Applications","container":"Chemical Reviews","year":2009}}]}
